When a recurring ARC task presents multiple demonstrations with changing colors, orientations, or boundary layouts, keep one cumulative ledger rather than inferring each example in isolation.

For each demo, compare input/output cell-by-cell and record:
- all changed coordinates and old/new values;
- any long edge stripe, short marker, compact prototype, or special region;
- exact alignment/orientation and the relation between structures;
- where changes start and stop, including marker endpoint treatment;
- same-looking but unchanged cells/components as negative evidence.

